From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:11:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] port fc27296d + b145a4a2: no O(n^2) tool-body rescans or
 partial-tag checks while streaming

fc27296d: inside a wrapped call the closing-tag search only looks at newly appended text (plus an overlap for a
tag split across feeds) until a candidate appears; then the original full walk runs for that call. Recovery
always uses the full walk. b145a4a2: _hold finds a held partial tag with str.find on the tag's first character
instead of testing every prefix of every tag. Both are exact (upstream's tests compare against the original walk
after every feed). Clean cherry-picks; tests test_parser_call_scan.py and test_parser_hold.py come along.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
